  "prediction": "**Tennis and Sports News**\n\nIn recent developments, tennis superstar Serena Williams has announced her return to training after a prolonged absence due to injury and illness. The 13-time Grand Slam champion, who has been ranked No. 10 in the latest rankings, has been practicing in Palm Beach Gardens since Tuesday. Williams had been on blood thinners for blood clots and had undergone an emergency procedure for a pulmonary embolism in February. Although she hasn't set a specific return date, her agent, Jill Smoller, stated that she will come back when she feels strong and healthy.\n\nMeanwhile, world No. 2 Kim Clijsters has suffered a freak foot accident that may keep her out of the French Open. Clijsters sustained severe strains and torn ligaments in her right ankle after taking a bad tumble at her cousin's wedding.\n\nIn other tennis news, Fort Lauderdale's Ryan Sweeting has won his first ATP title, defeating Kei Nishikori 6-4, 7-6 (7-3) in the U.S. Clay Court Championship in Houston. Sweeting, who was a wild card entry, moved up from No. 93 to No. 71 in the rankings.\n\nThe U.S. Fed Cup team will rely on 18-year-old Christina McHale and 19-year-old Melanie Oudin in a world group playoff against Germany this weekend. Despite being considered underdogs, the teenagers are expected to put up a strong fight.\n\n**Internet Archive News**\n\nIn a separate development, Alexa Internet has been donating its crawl data to the Internet Archive since 1996. The data, which flow in every day, are added to the Wayback Machine after an embargo period. This donation has helped to create a vast archive of the internet's history, providing a valuable resource for researchers and historians.\n\n**Key Dates**\n\n* May 22: French Open begins\n* Late June: Wimbledon\n* Late August: U.S. Open\n\n**Notable Players**\n\n* Serena Williams: 13-time Grand Slam champion, ranked No. 10\n* Kim Clijsters: world No. 2, out due to injury\n* Ryan Sweeting: won first ATP title, moved up to No. 71\n* Christina McHale: 18-year-old U.S. Fed Cup player\n* Melanie Oudin: 19-year-old U.S. Fed Cup player",
